cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use MicroRhodoDB, please cite it using the metadata in this file.
  No DOI has been minted for v1.6.1: cite the release version and the GitHub
  Release https://github.com/CongjianL/MicroRhodoDB/releases/tag/v1.6.1.
  A companion data-descriptor manuscript is in preparation for submission to
  Database (Oxford) or Scientific Data; this file will be updated with the
  paper citation once it is published.
title: >-
  MicroRhodoDB: a versioned, evidence-aware knowledgebase of Type-I microbial
  rhodopsins
type: dataset
version: 1.6.1
date-released: "2026-10-24"
authors:
  - given-names: CongJian
    family-names: Li
repository-code: "https://github.com/CongjianL/MicroRhodoDB"
url: "https://github.com/CongjianL/MicroRhodoDB/releases/tag/v1.6.1"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - microbial rhodopsins
  - Type-I rhodopsin
  - bacteriorhodopsin
  - phylogenomics
  - protein family database
  - UniProt
  - retinal-binding protein
  - xenorhodopsin
abstract: >-
  MicroRhodoDB curates 5,466 UniProtKB proteins carrying the Pfam domains
  PF01036/PF18761 and gives each an explicit, evidence-graded membership status
  (Type-I member, candidate, boundary family, heliorhodopsin outgroup, decoy),
  QC, redundancy, AlphaFold DB, retinal-pocket and GTDB taxonomy annotations, a
  placement on the MR_RT_003 reference tree (472 tips; 19 level-1 groups, of
  which 13 are named after characterised members and 6 carry provisional
  names), and a five-level function evidence ladder (E1 experimental to E5
  none) with the basis of every call, function-call conflict flags and linked
  publications. Engineered constructs are excluded from all counts, a
  family-HMM flag and a Foldseek watchlist point to novel families, every table
  and column is described in a data dictionary, and a read-only Python API, a
  command-line scorer and a static browser are provided. Releases are
  immutable, versioned SQLite databases with SHA-256 checksums. Version 1.6.1
  corrects 1.6.0 so that identical sequences share one membership status and
  one function call, marks provisional clade names, stops the command-line
  scorer from reporting heliorhodopsins as Type-I rhodopsins, and adds
  hard-negative, nearest-characterised-protein and replicate-tree validation
  analyses.
